<title>UK: ABBEY NATL SEES RATE DECISION BY FRIDAY.</title>
<headline>ABBEY NATL SEES RATE DECISION BY FRIDAY.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank Abbey National Plc said on Thursday it was reviewing interest rates after the Bank of England's rate rise and should reach a decision by Friday morning.</p>
<p>&quot;We should be announcing later this afternoon or tomorrow morning at the latest,&quot; a spokesman said.</p>
<p>The Bank of England raised UK interest rates to 7.00 percent from 6.75 percent. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
